}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1dbfdbd20e8aa7271ef733ba6f89247069237d0a48d7e8e129140dc55046dc0e","event_uuid":"e2c93c84-f1a9-4753-bed5-0f3fc964d7dd","position":{"commit_sha":"279d4236e14c289a9473b15e11d69711e44a7bfa","position":"1787374980799218001-e2c93c84-f1a9-4753-bed5-0f3fc964d7dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bc3f70b8e8ce6ed51950618621fb4f834764ac09e9962ed4af080d76e74b1540","event_uuid":"4b3ade40-75a7-474e-b737-bac1d759d3f8","position":{"commit_sha":"639b96c3ca2dea899c90bb9c4d0ec694dc2b8db7","position":"1787376632485177600-4b3ade40-75a7-474e-b737-bac1d759d3f8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-239_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e50ec61e-3a77-4eb8-b56b-c1d0f90ff9bc","comments":[],"created_at":1787374870148119001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"139df0ef-770e-4f64-b358-59c0a9d038d3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"},{"link_uuid":"4b3ade40-75a7-474e-b737-bac1d759d3f8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ffb5-c5ab-56a2-4ccf"}],"description":"## Problem\n`tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:201` still carries `xfail={\"mcp\": SCRATCHY}` on the\n`reason-close-obsolete` row, and `write_parity_contract.py:34-35` still describes it as \"the\nremaining scratchy-leprous-galago MCP gap\". But `scratchy-leprous-galago` (`1128-505b-54ac-497f`)\nis **closed**, so the live gap it points at is no longer tracked by any open ticket.\n\nThe gap is real: `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:223-232` `transition_ticket` accepts\n`ticket_id, current_status, target_status, close_class, force, caused_by, ref` and **not**\n`reason`, so a close whose justification is a `--reason` on a reason-required class cannot be\ndriven through MCP at all.\n\n## Why this is filed separately\nSurfaced while executing epic `2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a`, whose story `825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f` would\nhave closed it as part of a `TransitionRequest` consolidation. That story was unparented and\nclosed: converging the CLI/library reason rules is a behaviour change, not a de-duplication, and\ndid not belong in a consolidation epic. The MCP parity gap is independent of that decision and\nshould not disappear with it.\n\n## Trap recorded during that analysis\n`tests/interfaces/adapters.py:442-445` classifies via `self._tool_params(\"transition_ticket\")`\n**introspection**, so the strict-xfail flips to xpass the instant the parameter appears in the\nsignature — even if the body never forwards it. A signature-only addition would satisfy the\nmarker while the datum is still discarded, reproducing the `defiant-orthoclase-buck` failure\nmode one layer up. Only the oracle's `expected_status=\"closed\"` effect check catches that.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `transition_ticket` accepts `reason` and FORWARDS it to `rebar.transition`; checked by a test asserting the ticket actually reaches `closed` with its `close_reason` persisted, not merely that the parameter is exposed.\n- [ ] The `reason-close-obsolete` row passes on all three adapters and its `xfail={\"mcp\": SCRATCHY}` marker is deleted; checked by `pytest tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`.\n- [ ] The now-unused `SCRATCHY` constant and its stale comment at `write_parity_contract.py:34-36` are removed; checked by grep.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","ffb5-c5ab-56a2-4ccf"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2d9a1ecd-334d-48c2-9353-b60dd4214d7c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e1a2-0a03-e26b-416e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP transition_ticket still lacks 'reason'; its strict-xfail row outlives the closed bug that tracked it","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3a9db3dc-38d4-463a-82e6-faf4257c7871","139df0ef-770e-4f64-b358-59c0a9d038d3","2d9a1ecd-334d-48c2-9353-b60dd4214d7c","e2c93c84-f1a9-4753-bed5-0f3fc964d7dd","4b3ade40-75a7-474e-b737-bac1d759d3f8"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787378792773752813,"uuid":"7916f213-c6e9-44c7-b030-d73e9038c540"}